ments.
<span class=3D"code98">execv(3)</span> and friends are similar, except that=
 they use decayed arrays.</p>

<p>The complete exec family includes <span class=3D"code98">exec{l,le,lp,v,=
ve,vp}, fexecve(3),</span>
and if you=E2=80=99re using <span class=3D"code98">glibc</span>, the <span =
class=3D"code98">execvpe(3)</span> extension.</p>

<p>The family may be <i>invoked</i> in a way that allows you to specify a
command line string =E2=80=94 including, for example, together with <span c=
lass=3D"code98">sh(1)</span>:</p>

<p class=3D"bq"><span class=3D"code98">execl("/path/to/bin/sh", "sh", "-c",=
 command_line, (char *) NULL);</span></p>

<p>This is roughly how <span class=3D"code98">system(3)</span> is specified=
